  partName: Left Rear Sensor
  description: The Left Rear Sensor is a small, complex-shaped device positioned
    at the bottom-left-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible
    for monitoring critical engine parameters such as temperature, pressure, or vibration.
    This sensor provides vital data to the engine control unit, enabling optimal
    engine performance and efficiency. One interesting aspect of the Left Rear Sensor
    is its ability to operate accurately in extreme temperatures and environments.
